<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Gaugamela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">331 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Gaugamela · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-alexander-the-great">Wars of Alexander the Great</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Gaugamela was fought in 331 BCE in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> and the Achaemenid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a>. Despite being outnumbered, Alexander won a decisive victory and Darius fled. The battle led to the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> and its conquest by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela.jpg" alt="Battle of Gaugamela" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pietro da Cortona · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pietro_da_Cortona_-_Battle_of_Alexander_versus_Darius_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
